desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Template Unescaped With Safe"
	title_zh: "检测到Template Unescaped With Safe",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-template-unescaped-with-safe"
	risk: "xss"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `template-unescaped-with-safe` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/python/flask/security/xss/audit/template-unescaped-with-safe.yaml).
Original message: Detected a segment of a Flask template where autoescaping is explicitly disabled with '| safe' filter. This allows rendering of raw HTML in this segment. Ensure no user data is rendered here, otherwise this is a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- https://flask.palletsprojects.com/en/1.1.x/security/#cross-site-scripting-xss
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.html": <<<POS
{{3"G$5y|	safe

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.html}.pattern_regex(/{{.*?\|\s*safe(\s*}})?/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Template Unescaped With Safe",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Unescaped With Safe",
	message: "Template Unescaped With Safe",
}
